From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - fix the AEAD fallback calling itself

aead_do_fallback() sets up the subrequest for the software fallback
but then passes the original request to crypto_aead_encrypt() and
crypto_aead_decrypt(). That calls back into aead_encrypt() or
aead_decrypt() of this driver, which picks the fallback again, so the
call recurses until the stack overflows.

Any request that needs the fallback takes this path, for example AES-GCM
or AES-CCM with no AAD and no plaintext. That is the first gcm(aes)
self-test vector, so loading the driver with the self-tests enabled
crashes the kernel.

Pass the subrequest instead.

Fixes: 654627ad0bee ("crypto: bcm - Use subrequest for fallback")

Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/cipher.c
@@ -2595,8 +2595,8 @@ static int aead_do_fallback(struct aead_request *req, bool is_encrypt)
 			       req->iv);
 	aead_request_set_ad(subreq, req->assoclen);
 
-	return is_encrypt ? crypto_aead_encrypt(req) :
-			    crypto_aead_decrypt(req);
+	return is_encrypt ? crypto_aead_encrypt(subreq) :
+			    crypto_aead_decrypt(subreq);
 }
 
 static int aead_enqueue(struct aead_request *req, bool is_encrypt)
